<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS privacy strings for RichOS.

  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription is REQUIRED for voice mode: without it macOS denies the
  TCC microphone grant and CoreAudio hands the process an endless stream of zeros rather
  than an error — a silent failure that looks like "Rich can't hear me" with nothing in
  any log. The string below is what the CEO reads in the system prompt, so it is written
  in Rich's voice, not in engineering's.

  Tauri 2 merges this file into the bundled app's generated Info.plist. It is NOT applied
  to a bare `cargo run` binary, which has no bundle to carry it — a dev run inherits the
  TCC grant of whatever launched it.

  FLAGGED FOR THE PACKAGING ENGINEER (next round): please verify this merge actually lands
  in `RichOS.app/Contents/Info.plist` after `cargo tauri build`, and that the hardened
  runtime entitlement `com.apple.security.device.audio-input` is present in the signing
  entitlements — notarized, hardened-runtime apps need BOTH the usage string and the
  entitlement. Neither is verified here: this machine has no microphone to test the grant
  against (see app/crates/richos-voice/src/capture.rs).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Rich listens when you tap the talk button, so you can speak to him instead of typing. Nothing is recorded or sent anywhere — speech is turned into text on this Mac.</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
